<?xml version="1.0" encoding="utf-8"?>
<Defs>

  <!--
    Big, point-scaled threats. RaidEnemy's squad composition/tactic (points and tech spent against the
    raiding faction's own PawnGroupMakers/RaidStrategyDefs) lives in IncidentWorker_RaidEnemy; see that
    class's doc comment for exactly how far it goes without a Map to place the squad on. ManhunterPack has
    its own worker now (IncidentWorker_ManhunterPack); it spends its points on pack size and turns the pack
    among the settlement rather than marching it in from an edge, for the reason that class's doc gives.

    Weights and refire from RimWorld (rimworldwiki.com "Events", event data table, read for playtest-bugs4; not
    checked against a decompile): RaidEnemy chance 9.0 and no wait between repeats, ManhunterPack chance 2.0 and
    15 days before it may repeat. They were 1.0 and 0.5 with no wait, so a pack was a third of the big threats
    rather than RimWorld's fifth, and while no rival can raid yet (a lone tribe early in the arc, before any
    neighbour is hostile) every big threat was a pack: the third playtest's letter pile was mostly maddened
    beasts. With the wait, a lone tribe meets a pack at most every 15 days and the rest of its big-threat
    rolls come up empty, which is what RimWorld's own selection does when nothing in the category can fire.
  -->

  <IncidentDef>
    <defName>RaidEnemy</defName>
    <label>raid</label>
    <description>Hostiles attack the civilization.</description>
    <category>ThreatBig</category>
    <targetTags><li>Map_PlayerHome</li></targetTags>
    <workerClass>SimWorld.Director.IncidentWorker_RaidEnemy</workerClass>
    <baseChance>9.0</baseChance>
    <minThreatPoints>35</minThreatPoints>
    <pointsScaleable>true</pointsScaleable>
  </IncidentDef>

  <IncidentDef>
    <defName>ManhunterPack</defName>
    <label>maddened beasts</label>
    <description>A pack of animals is driven mad and attacks the civilization.</description>
    <category>ThreatBig</category>
    <targetTags><li>Map_PlayerHome</li></targetTags>
    <workerClass>SimWorld.Director.IncidentWorker_ManhunterPack</workerClass>
    <baseChance>2.0</baseChance>
    <minRefireDays>15</minRefireDays>
    <minThreatPoints>35</minThreatPoints>
    <pointsScaleable>true</pointsScaleable>
  </IncidentDef>

</Defs>
